I("Sposob dzialania mdfsa bierze to pod uwage",
  "We thank the Reviewer. MDFS discretises each feature independently into bins and evaluates the information that the resulting bin memberships carry about the label; it does not assume additivity, linearity or any particular scale of the data, and a monotone transformation of a feature (for example a centred log-ratio transform applied feature by feature) does not change its binning. The compositional constraint nevertheless means that a dependence between two features can partly reflect the shared constraint of the simplex rather than a biological relationship; the log-ratio encoding of a pair is scale-invariant and unaffected by this constraint, whereas the geometric mean is not. We now discuss this in the Limitations and note that it is one of the reasons why the ecological interpretations are presented as hypotheses.",
  NOTE + " Your note says that the way MDFS works takes compositionality into account; I wrote a cautious version. Please check it with Prof. Rudnicki, in particular the claim that per-feature monotone transforms do not change the discretisation (true for quantile-based cut points, which is my understanding of the MDFS discretisation).")
